Query the submit button with `screen.getByRole('button', { name: /submit|log in/i })` — that's how a user or screen reader identifies it, by its accessible role and visible label, not by an internal test id. Drive the click with user-event rather than fireEvent: `const user = userEvent.setup(); await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /submit/i }));`. For the error message, since it appears asynchronously after the click triggers validation, use `await screen.findByText(/password is required/i)` (or `findByRole('alert', ...)` if the error is rendered with an alert role) rather than a synchronous `getByText`, since `findBy*` retries until the DOM updates. Putting it together:
```tsx
const user = userEvent.setup();
render(<LoginForm />);
await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /submit/i }));
expect(await screen.findByText(/password is required/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
```
Only fall back to `data-testid` if the button or error text genuinely has no accessible role/label/text to query by.
